WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.840
Welcome to Genoa, a beautiful port city in
the north of Italy.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.109
It's a very vertical city, built on a lot
of hills.

00:00:07.109 --> 00:00:11.360
So many hills, in fact, that the city has
several funicular railways and elevators

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.030
tunnelled through the rock, shortcuts that
get around

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.170
miles of twisty, congested roads or thousands
of stairs.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.500
And the strangest one of these is the Ascensore
Castello d'Albertis Montegalleto.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.039
Or: the castle elevator.

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:29.539
Years ago, you'd have to walk through 300m
of tunnel yourself to reach the lift,

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:31.250
but now, if you start at the bottom,

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.370
an odd little square box comes to pick you
up.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.300
It looks a bit like a regular elevator car,
only going horizontally.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.300
You get on, it takes you the 300 metres through
the rock,

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.100
past some control equipment and then,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.059
after a bit of shunting around with another
box that's headed the other way...

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:48.440
It goes vertically,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.289
right up to the castle at the top of the hill.

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:53.629
Now you might think, that's a great idea in
theory,

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:56.090
it's like a Star Trek turbolift, but surely
that's dangerous?

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:58.770
And I say that wearing a red shirt.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.670
Elevators need to have all sorts of protection
systems

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:04.330
so one bad cable can't snap and cause disaster.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.340
How can they possibly make one that has all
that protection

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.030
when it's got to detach itself and move off?

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.590
The answer is: they can't. Because that's
not what it's doing.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.990
And in hindsight, the solution is kind of
obvious:

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.310
there are two separate systems here.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:23.840
It's the same hack that Disney use for the
Tower of Terror at their theme parks:

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:27.570
the bit that the passengers get into can only
go horizontally on its own.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.060
It attaches to a cable that pulls it along.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.790
When it reaches the lift shaft,

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.180
it's actually getting into another, bigger
elevator,

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.340
it attaches itself firmly to that,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.540
and then it gets hoisted up and down in safety

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.479
as if it were a regular passenger elevator.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:44.119
It's a brilliant bit of engineering.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:48.249
And it's all so people don't have to walk
300 metres to a regular lift.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.320
